    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Summary",
      "html": "<p>This optional unit adds 50 words that occur 19–22 times in the New Testament and are not in Machen&#x27;s lessons: 23 nouns, 20 verbs and 7 other words. Nothing in the course waits for them; they are here so that you can read the New Testament with the lexicon open less often. Learn them on the Words track: recognize, recall, type, type with accents.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Built from words you know",
      "html": "<p>These verbs are a preposition plus a verb from the lessons; the meaning usually follows from the parts: ἐφίστημι (ἵστημι); καθίστημι (ἵστημι); ὑπακούω (ἀκούω); προάγω (ἄγω); ἀπέχω (ἔχω); διακρίνω (κρίνω); ἐπαίρω (αἴρω).</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Common confusion",
      "html": "<p>Look-alikes that differ by one letter: βασιλεύω (I rule) and βασιλεύς (a king).</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Source",
      "html": "<p>Words chosen by their New Testament frequency (MorphGNT); glosses after Jeffrey Dodson&#x27;s Greek-English lexicon (public domain).</p>"
    },
